{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2664","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2664","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2664\",\"parent_revision\":\"7d3c9112a2be45b8a2bdd0a62f531fe6e684b728e2ebcb4bb10a1057ebfcc1f5\",\"root_revision\":\"7d3c9112a2be45b8a2bdd0a62f531fe6e684b728e2ebcb4bb10a1057ebfcc1f5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-07-08\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_view(selector=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` routes through `find_item(parse_backlog(), selector)` in `operations.py:3411`. `parse_backlog()` loads the local YAML cache. For beads nanoid selectors, `parse_issue_selector` returns `None` (not numeric), so the `view_enrich_from_github` path \u2014 which for BeadsBackend calls `bd show <id>` directly \u2014 is never reached.\\n\\nResult: the nanoid selector only works if the beads item has already been pulled into the local YAML cache. If the item exists only in the beads DB and has not been pulled locally, `backlog_view` raises `ItemNotFoundError`.\\n\\nFor the GitHub backend this design makes sense \u2014 items are remote and cached locally. For the beads backend, items are always local (beads is a local Dolt DB), so the cache intermediary is unnecessary overhead and a reliability gap. The direct lookup path (`bd show <id>`) exists in `BeadsBackend.view_enrich_from_github` at `beads_backend.py:463` but is only called when the selector is a numeric ID, not a nanoid.\\n\\nObserved: an agent called `backlog_view` with a beads nanoid and received no result, then worked around it by embedding the bead content directly in phase prompts. Documented in session log `dh-with-bd-example.txt` (2026-06-19), line 2478.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:17:01.889182Z</sub>\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: `parse_issue_selector` returns None for beads nanoids like \\\"bd-a3f8\\\"\\nevidence: parsing.py:284-310 handles only GitHub URL, `#N`, and bare number; nanoid \\\"bd-a3f8\\\" matches none of these patterns; function returns None\\nsource: File: parsing.py:284-310\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: The `view_enrich_from_github` enrichment path in `backlog_view` is gated by `if issue_num:` where `issue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)`\\nevidence: operations.py:3412 `issue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)`; operations.py:3415 `if issue_num:` \u2014 enrichment only called when parse_issue_selector returns non-None\\nsource: File: operations.py:3411-3427\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: `BeadsBackend.view_enrich_from_github` at beads_backend.py:463 accepts string nanoid IDs and calls `bd show <id>` directly\\nevidence: beads_backend.py:463 `def view_enrich_from_github(self, result: ViewItemResult, issue_num: str, repo: str = \\\"\\\") -> bool`; body calls `self._runner.run_json([\\\"show\\\", issue_num])`; unit tests at test_beads_backend.py:659-740 confirm this\\nsource: File: beads_backend.py:463-495, test_beads_backend.py:659-740\\n\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: `issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\"` property is available on the backend protocol and set to \\\"string\\\" on BeadsBackend\\nevidence: backend_protocol.py:210 `issue_id_type: Literal[\\\"integer\\\", \\\"string\\\"]`; beads_backend.py:159 `issue_id_type: Literal[\\\"integer\\\", \\\"string\\\"] = \\\"string\\\"`\\nsource: File: backend_protocol.py:210, beads_backend.py:159\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:16:15.661671Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: backlog_view with beads nanoid selector only works if item is in local cache\\nDate: 2026-06-21\\nGoal: Fix backlog_view to resolve beads nanoid selectors directly via bd show when item is not in local YAML cache.\\nConditions:\\n1. Bug location \u2014 operations.py::backlog_view (lines 3411\u20133427) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File: operations.py:3411-3427 \u2014 `elif not item: raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)` reached when both find_item and parse_issue_selector return None\\n2. parse_issue_selector returns None for beads nanoids | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File: parsing.py:284-310 \u2014 only handles GitHub URL, #N, bare number; nanoids match none\\n3. BeadsBackend.view_enrich_from_github accepts string nanoid IDs | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File: beads_backend.py:463-495, test_beads_backend.py:659-740\\n4. issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\" property exists on BackendProtocol and BeadsBackend | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File: backend_protocol.py:210, beads_backend.py:159\\n5. No existing test for backlog_view + uncached beads nanoid | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Command: grep backlog_view tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py \u2014 no test covers this path\\nChanges from snapshot: None\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **backlog_view with beads nanoid selector only works if item is in local cache** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Source code analysis \u2014 operations.py:3411, beads_backend.py:463, parsing.py:find_item (2026-06-20)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-21)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:18:25.123997Z</sub>\\n\\n**Environment**: beads backend (issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\")\\n**Precondition**: beads item exists in beads DB but has NOT been pulled into local YAML cache (no `bd pull` / `backlog_pull` run since creation)\\n**Steps**:\\n1. Configure backend=beads\\n2. Create a beads item: `bd create \\\"Fix authentication bug\\\"` \u2014 note returned nanoid (e.g., \\\"bd-a3f8\\\")\\n3. Do NOT run `bd pull` or `backlog_pull`\\n4. Call `backlog_view(selector=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` via MCP\\n**Expected**: ViewItemResult populated from beads DB via `bd show bd-a3f8`\\n**Actual**: ItemNotFoundError(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\") raised\\n**Note**: If `bd pull` is run first (pulling item into local YAML cache), the bug does not manifest \u2014 `find_item` matches by string-ID equality from the cache. Bug is specific to the uncached path.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:18:42.252223Z</sub>\\n\\n**Level**: P1\\n**Rationale**: Agents on the beads backend cannot reliably view items via the standard `backlog_view` MCP interface. The only known workaround is embedding item content directly in prompts (observed in session log 2026-06-19 line 2478), which bypasses the standardized tool interface, increases prompt size, and reduces reliability.\\n**Urgency**: High \u2014 affects all beads-backend workflows where items are viewed before the first `bd pull`\\n**Effort**: S\\n</div>\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:19:22.548250Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen the active backend is beads (`issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\"`) and the selector is a beads nanoid (e.g., \\\"bd-a3f8\\\") that is not in the local YAML cache, `backlog_view` should attempt `view_enrich_from_github(result, selector, repo)` directly. On success (beads returns item data), the enriched ViewItemResult is returned. On failure (beads cannot find the item), ItemNotFoundError is raised with the original selector. Existing paths \u2014 numeric GitHub selectors, title-substring searches, and cached beads items \u2014 are unchanged.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:19:02.984414Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(selector=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` returns enriched ViewItemResult when item exists in beads DB but NOT in local YAML cache\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(selector=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` raises ItemNotFoundError when item does not exist in beads DB (bd show returns non-zero exit code)\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#2664\\\")` continues to work correctly for GitHub numeric selectors (no regression)\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(selector=\\\"some title\\\")` continues to work for title-substring searches (no regression)\\n- [ ] `backlog_view(selector=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` continues to work when item IS in local cache (no regression)\\n- [ ] New test added in tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py: beads backend, nanoid selector, item absent from local cache \u2192 enrichment called, result returned\\n</div>\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:19:54.954357Z</sub>\\n\\n- operations.py:3411-3427 \u2014 backlog_view routing gate (fix location)\\n- beads_backend.py:463-495 \u2014 view_enrich_from_github (already handles nanoid strings; no change needed)\\n- backend_protocol.py:210 \u2014 issue_id_type property (detection mechanism for string-ID backends)\\n- parsing.py:284-310 \u2014 parse_issue_selector (intentionally numeric-only; no change needed)\\n- test_beads_backend.py:659-740 \u2014 existing view_enrich_from_github tests (reference for new test)\\n</div>\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:19:38.273546Z</sub>\\n\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 fix location: add string-ID backend fallback path in `backlog_view` (lines 3411\u20133427)\\n- `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` \u2014 new test: `test_backlog_view_beads_nanoid_not_in_local_cache`\\n</div>\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:20:10.317673Z</sub>\\n\\nNone. The fix is self-contained in `operations.py::backlog_view`. The required detection mechanism (`backend.issue_id_type`) and enrichment implementation (`BeadsBackend.view_enrich_from_github`) already exist. No new dependencies, protocol changes, or schema migrations required.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:20:27.544897Z</sub>\\n\\nEffort: S (Small, < 2 hours)\\n- Code: ~10\u201320 lines in operations.py::backlog_view \u2014 add string-ID backend fallback path in the `elif not item:` branch\\n- Test: 1 new test case in tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py\\n- No schema changes, no protocol changes, no migration\\n</div>\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- Any MCP caller using `backlog_view(selector=\\\"bd-xxxx\\\")` on the beads backend \u2014 currently receives `ItemNotFoundError` instead of enriched result; fixed callers receive correct data\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `backlog_core/backends/beads_backend.py::view_enrich_from_github` \u2014 no change needed; already accepts and handles nanoid strings correctly\\n- `backlog_core/backend_protocol.py::issue_id_type` \u2014 `Literal[\\\"integer\\\", \\\"string\\\"]` detection property used in fix; no change needed\\n- `backlog_core/parsing.py::parse_issue_selector` \u2014 intentionally numeric-only; no change needed; fix works around its limitation\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::backlog_view` \u2014 routing gate (`if issue_num:`) must also attempt `view_enrich_from_github` for string-ID selectors when item is absent from local cache\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:18:03.406750Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED (post-fix)\\n\\nThe design intent of `backlog_view` is to return live-enriched item data from the active backend, falling back to local cache when the backend is unreachable. For string-ID backends (beads), the enrichment path is already correctly implemented in `BeadsBackend.view_enrich_from_github`. The bug is a missing routing branch in the orchestrating function (operations.py), not a design conflict. The fix adds the missing branch using the existing `issue_id_type` capability flag \u2014 restoring alignment between design intent and implementation. No design change is required.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `backlog_core/operations.py::backlog_view` docstring \u2014 should note beads nanoid selector support after fix\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n</div>\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:16:39.531260Z</sub>\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:17:19.634052Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n**Rationale**: Traceable failure chain in source code \u2014 backlog_view computes `issue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)` which returns None for beads nanoids; the enrichment gate `if issue_num:` is never entered; `elif not item: raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)` is reached. All links observable in operations.py:3411-3427.\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys\\n**Scenario Target**: Agent calls `backlog_view(selector=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` on beads backend when item not pulled to local cache \u2192 ItemNotFoundError \u2192 agent cannot read item via standard MCP interface \u2192 workaround embeds item content directly in prompts\\n</div>\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-06-21T08:17:44.448685Z</sub>\\n\\n5-whys chain:\\n\\n1. Why does `backlog_view(selector=\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` raise ItemNotFoundError when item not in local cache?\\n   \u2192 `item = find_item(parse_backlog(), selector)` returns None (not in cache). `issue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)` returns None (nanoid is not #N/URL/number). Branch `elif not item: raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)` is reached.\\n   Evidence: operations.py:3411-3427\\n\\n2. Why does `parse_issue_selector(\\\"bd-a3f8\\\")` return None?\\n   \u2192 parse_issue_selector handles only GitHub URL, `#N`, and bare integer forms. Beads nanoids (\\\"bd-xxxx\\\") match none of these. Function was designed before the beads string-ID backend existed.\\n   Evidence: parsing.py:284-310\\n\\n3. Why doesn't backlog_view fall through to call view_enrich_from_github with the raw selector?\\n   \u2192 The `if issue_num:` gate equates \\\"should we enrich from backend?\\\" with \\\"did parse_issue_selector return a numeric value?\\\". For string-ID backends, parse_issue_selector always returns None \u2014 enrichment is never attempted, even though BeadsBackend fully supports it.\\n   Evidence: operations.py:3415\\n\\n4. Why does BeadsBackend.view_enrich_from_github already accept string IDs correctly?\\n   \u2192 It was implemented correctly from the start (beads_backend.py:463-495, tests at test_beads_backend.py:659-740). The failure is in the routing logic in operations.py, not in the enrichment implementation.\\n   Evidence: beads_backend.py:463-495\\n\\nRoot design cause: backlog_view conflates \\\"extract numeric ID from selector\\\" with \\\"should we call view_enrich_from_github?\\\". For string-ID backends, these are separate questions \u2014 no numeric ID exists, but backend enrichment is both necessary and already implemented. The routing gate needs a separate path using the existing `backend.issue_id_type` capability flag.\\n\\nFix pattern: When `issue_num` is None AND `item` is None, check `get_config().backend.issue_id_type == \\\"string\\\"` and attempt `view_enrich_from_github(result, selector.strip(), repo)` directly. Uses existing infrastructure with no protocol changes required.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `operations.py::backlog_view` \u2014 primary fix location; routes selector to backend enrichment or local cache\\n- `beads_backend.py::view_enrich_from_github` \u2014 already correct; accepts string nanoids; no change\\n- `backend_protocol.py::issue_id_type` \u2014 capability flag used to detect string-ID backends\\n- `parsing.py::parse_issue_selector` \u2014 numeric-only by design; fix does not require changes here\\n\",\"digest\":\"a2cdb4386b81a95484eea3b5563d76329052edd0e404f847ee88e3210503fdb6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCJhXg\"}"}